Source: libdiag
Maintainer: Agathe Porte <agathe.porte@oss.qualcomm.com>
Standards-Version: 4.7.4
Section: non-free/misc
Build-Depends:
 debhelper-compat (= 13),
Build-Depends-Arch:
 libglib2.0-0t64,
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/qualcomm-linux/pkg-libdiag
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/qualcomm-linux/pkg-libdiag.git

Package: libdiag1
Architecture: arm64
Description: Qualcomm Diag framework (runtime library)
 Qualcomm Diag is a specialized communication interface built into Qualcomm
 chipsets. It exposes low-level baseband, network logging, and device
 calibration features to engineers and repair tools via a virtual COM port.
 .
 This package provides the runtime library.
Section: non-free/libs
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},

Package: libdiag-dev
Architecture: arm64
Description: Qualcomm Diag framework (development files)
 Qualcomm Diag is a specialized communication interface built into Qualcomm
 chipsets. It exposes low-level baseband, network logging, and device
 calibration features to engineers and repair tools via a virtual COM port.
 .
 This package provides files necessary to develop programs using the library.
Section: non-free/libdevel
Depends:
 libdiag1 (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},

Package: qcom-diag
Architecture: arm64
Description: Qualcomm Diag framework (tools)
 Qualcomm Diag is a specialized communication interface built into Qualcomm
 chipsets. It exposes low-level baseband, network logging, and device
 calibration features to engineers and repair tools via a virtual COM port.
 .
 This package provides diagnostic tools and utilities using the library.
Section: non-free/utils
Depends:
